{
  "title": "An honest but unrepaired inconsistency escalates, never freezes",
  "description": "Dana is who she says she is (every live check stays clean the whole call) but, well past the correction window and without any correction or negation language, names a different deadline than she gave at the top of the call. The ledger records this as CONTRADICTED, not CORRECTED -- there is no mechanic for \"explained it to my satisfaction\" to erase a logged inconsistency. Because every live check still passes, freeze rule 7b (contradiction AND a failed check) never fires -- this is precisely why the rulebook separates STORY_INCONSISTENCY-alone from FREEZE: a caller with a clean identity and a messy story still needs a human, but does not get treated as an active attacker.",
